Tom Jackson, who parlayed a 14-season stint as a stalwart linebacker on the Denver Broncos&#x2019; famed &#x201C;Orange Crush&#x201D; defense into a career as a popular football analyst on ESPN , has died. He was 75.

Jackson died Friday, his family told the network. No other details of his death were immediately available.

Jackson was best known for his work alongside Chris Berman on the ESPN shows NFL Primetime and Sunday NFL Countdown , where the pair would deliver their humorous, entertaining take on highlights from games. Related Stories Music Peak Halftime Show: The A-List Machine Eventizing Pro Games Movies Lance Broadway, Pitcher Turned 'Olympus Has Fallen' Actor, Dies at 43

&#x201C;All of us are stunned,&#x201D; Berman said in a statement. &#x201C;I&#x2019;m stunned, we&#x2019;re stunned and you&#x2019;re stunned. We&#x2019;ve lost one of the best human beings ever to walk the planet, Tom Jackson. I was fortunate to work side by side with Tom for 30 years &#x2026; It was a labor of love for our whole team, both in front of the camera and behind it. We always hoped our viewers enjoyed the shows as much as we did bringing it to them every week.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Berman said on Sunday NFL Countdown that Jackson&#x2019;s death was unexpected and that he spoke with his best friend &#x201C;at length&#x201D; on Tuesday. &#x201C;He was a vital 75,&#x201D; he said.

&#x201C;Tom was so much more than an accomplished NFL analyst,&#x201D; he said in his statement. &#x201C;There was nobody kinder, more thoughtful, more loyal or more engaging than him. And when it came to laughter, Tom&#x2019;s was frequent and unmistakable. He is easily summed up by this classic old song: &#x2018;He&#x2019;s got sunshine on a cloudy day.&#x2019;&#x201D;

Added ESPN chairman Jimmy Pitaro: &#x201C;He brought the credibility of an All-Pro NFL player, the insight of a gifted analyst and a warmth and authenticity that connected with generations of football fans.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

ESPN&#x2019;s NFL studio is named the Chris Berman-Tom Jackson Studio.

A fourth-round pick by the Broncos in the 1973 NFL Draft out of the University of Louisville, Jackson played in 191 regular-season games, the most in team history when he retired in 1986, and 10 playoff games, all with Denver.

He was a first-team All Pro in 1977 and 1978, and a three-time Pro Bowl selection, and he was inducted into the team&#x2019;s Ring of Fame in 1992.

When he retired at 36, he was the NFL&#x2019;s oldest linebacker.

&#x201C;An inspirational leader and fierce competitor, TJ was a proud member of the Broncos&#x2019; first Super Bowl team [in 1977] that helped establish a winning tradition in Denver,&#x201D; the team said in a statement. &#x201C;Off the field, Tom carried himself with class, warmth and humility, forging deep connections and lifelong friendships with teammates and throughout Broncos Country.&#x201D;

Jackson, who joined ESPN in 1987, was awarded the Pete Rozelle Radio-Television Award by the Pro Football Hall of Fame in 2015. He retired from broadcasting a year later but reunited with Berman for a digital-only edition of NFL Primetime in 2019.

He often said that he had been &#x201C;blessed to work for two companies in my life: the Denver Broncos and ESPN.&#x201D;

Survivors include his wife, Jennifer, and his daughters, Taylor and Morgan.

&#x201C; The Unknown &#x201D; filmmaker Arthur Harari says AI is a &#x201C;slippery slope&#x201D; and one he&#x2019;d prefer to avoid in his own work &#x2014; even as he admitted on Sunday at the Marrakech Film Festival that he used a deepfake tool in his Palme d&#x2019;Or contender, a body-swap psychodrama starring L&#xE9;a Seydoux.

Appearing in conversation with film critic and historian Charles Tesson, the Oscar-winning &#x201C;Anatomy of a Fall&#x201D; co-writer was asked by an audience member how he viewed the role of AI technology in his creative process. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Tallinn Black Nights Fest Awards: ‘On Top of the Cliff’ Scores Grand Prix, ’When She Hears the Bells’ Bags Best First Feature ‘Four Minus Three’ Takes Cairo Film Festival’s Golden Pyramid, While ‘Summer Meadow’ Wins Three Awards and ‘The Day of Wrath’ Nabs Two

&#x201C;I&#x2019;m in much the same position as everyone else: this shift toward using AI is suddenly upon us, and it&#x2019;s becoming not just a possibility, but something increasingly pervasive and tempting,&#x201D; Harari said. &#x201C;Personally, I&#x2019;ve never used it; for the time being, I don&#x2019;t see any place for it in my work.&#x201D;

The acclaimed writer-director went on to walk that statement back moments later, when he admitted that his team employed deepfake technology for a pivotal scene in his latest film.

&#x201C;At one point in &#x2018;The Unknown,&#x2019; there is a scene where L&#xE9;a Seydoux kisses L&#xE9;a Seydoux, and we had to use a deepfake tool to do that,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;But there was a human behind it. There was always a human involved &#x2014; someone who programs it, so to speak, and keeps it under control. So, I&#x2019;m not against it in principle. It&#x2019;s just that I think we need to ask ourselves what constitutes the essence of what we&#x2019;re trying to create &#x2014; right from the writing stage.&#x201D;

As a writer, Harari appeared to be more resistant to the technology, conceding that AI tools were &#x201C;perfectly legitimate and interesting&#x201D; when it comes to performing simple research tasks. But to go beyond that &#x2014; &#x201C;to actually craft parts of the writing process&#x201D; &#x2014; was, he insisted, &#x201C;a very slippery slope.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;The thing is, we are inherently prone to addiction &#x2014; look at our phones, for instance; we&#x2019;re constantly glued to them,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;Once you get a foot in the door, it becomes incredibly difficult not to use it at every turn.&#x201D;

Premiering in competition at this year&#x2019;s Cannes Film Festival, &#x201C;The Unknown&#x201D; stars Seydoux as an unknown woman who has a one-night stand with a photographer named David (Niels Schneider). When David wakes up, he&#x2019;s trapped inside Seydoux&#x2019;s body. The film was based on a graphic novel co-written by Harari.

Speaking to Variety earlier this year, the French actress described the role as &#x201C;the best part I&#x2019;ve ever played.&#x201D; Asked if she thought AI would put filmmakers out of business, she replied, &#x201C;I don&#x2019;t think so. I think that nothing can replace humanity. I don&#x2019;t feel threatened. Maybe I&#x2019;m wrong! But I believe in human nature.&#x201D;

Harari is on hand at the Marrakech Film Festival as part of its popular Conversation series. He's appearing alongside &#x201C;Knives Out&#x201D; director Rian Johnson, &#x201C;Call Me by Your Name&#x201D; Oscar nominee Luca Guadagnino, &#x201C;Fjord&#x201D; Palme d&#x2019;Or winner Cristian Mungiu, Italian screen icon Monica Bellucci and more.

The Marrakech Film Festival runs Nov. 20&#x2013;28.

When filmmaker James Gray was a teenager, he wrote a fan letter to Francis Ford Coppola . To his surprise, the legendary filmmaker wrote back with a piece of advice that would come to shape Gray&#x2019;s entire approach to cinema.

&#x201C;He said, &#x2018;Be personal, James. There&#x2019;s only one of you in this world,&#x2019;&#x201D; Gray recalled during a press conference Sunday at the Doha Film Festival . &#x201C;I&#x2019;ve tried to take that to heart, that if I have anything to say at all, if I have a voice that matters at all, it&#x2019;s best that I become as personal as I can.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Disney Inks Deal With Creator Zach King for 'Illusion Shorts' Inspired by Mouse House's Movies and Experiences Disney Expected to Lay Off Thousands of Staffers in Biggest Round of Cuts This Year

Decades later, that philosophy remains central to Gray&#x2019;s filmmaking, even as he argues that the film industry increasingly pressures directors to suppress their individual voices.

&#x201C;So much of the system, the systems in the cinema, both in the United States and abroad, try to discourage you from your own voice,&#x201D; he said. &#x201C;Or, if they don&#x2019;t discourage you actively, they try to get you to bury your voice in a larger statement, or another form of genre, where it&#x2019;s hidden.&#x201D;

The director was in Doha to present the MENA premiere of &#x201C; Paper Tiger ,&#x201D; his latest crime drama starring Adam Driver, Miles Teller and Scarlett Johansson. Set in 1980s New York, the film follows two brothers whose pursuit of the American Dream draws them into a dangerous scheme involving the Russian mafia.

Drawing heavily on his own family history, Gray described the film as an attempt to faithfully capture his father&#x2019;s relationship with his uncle, while acknowledging the possible limitations of his own memory years later. He also recalled how a confrontation between his parents found its way into the film, with the actors recreating the incident almost exactly as it had unfolded in real life. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Although &#x201C;Paper Tiger&#x201D; is framed as a crime drama, Gray said he does not think of his films primarily in terms of genre, which he sees as a way of categorizing cinema rather than defining its true purpose.

&#x201C;I&#x2019;m just telling my story as best I can, as clearly as I can, as honestly as I can, and I hope for the best,&#x201D; he said. For Gray, that commitment to honesty is also a means of fostering compassion and understanding. &#x201C;That is how we extend the idea of compassion and sympathy in this world,&#x201D; he explained. &#x201C;Hopefully you can see something in me that matters to you.&#x201D;

&#x201C;I have been very lucky to be able to pursue a cinema which is very directly personal,&#x201D; he added. &#x201C;So I don&#x2019;t take it lightly. It&#x2019;s a responsibility I take very seriously. And I think it&#x2019;s actually the true calling of the filmmaker.&#x201D;

The conversation also turned to the future of independent cinema, with Brazilian producer Rodrigo Teixeira, whose &#x201C;Paper Tiger&#x201D; and &#x201C;Furies&#x201D; are both screening in Doha, pushing back against concerns about the dominance of Hollywood blockbusters.

&#x201C;You&#x2019;re always going to have space to create original films outside of the system, because it&#x2019;s impossible to own the whole system, even with all these mergers,&#x201D; Teixeira said, citing companies such as A24 and Neon as examples of how independent filmmaking continues to thrive.

Drawing a comparison between filmmaking in Brazil and the U.S., Teixeira argued that independent producers face much the same challenges regardless of geography. The principal difference, he said, is the public funding available in his home country, where federal support for cinema has long helped sustain the industry.

&#x201C;We have a government who supports cinema, who supports art,&#x201D; he said, contrasting Brazil&#x2019;s system with the U.S., where comparable government support is absent.

Gray, meanwhile, recalled that he once believed cinema might follow the trajectory of opera, flourishing for roughly a century before eventually being eclipsed by another art form. While he acknowledged that cinema faces growing competition from video games and other forms of entertainment, and described the dominance of the blockbuster model as &#x201C;overall quite harmful.&#x201D; But the increasing accessibility of filmmaking technology has begun to challenge his earlier pessimism. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#x201C;I have a kind of optimism about the availability of technology and how that will introduce new voices.&#x201D;
